# GardenPulse API — manual requests
#
# Open this file in VS Code with the REST Client extension (humao.rest-client)
# and click "Send Request" above any request. Start the API first: npm run dev

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### Health check → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Unknown route → 404 NotFound
GET {{baseUrl}}/does-not-exist

### Malformed JSON body → 400 InvalidJSON
POST {{baseUrl}}/health
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name":

### Register a user → 201 (a second run → 409 Conflict)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ada Gardener",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "plain-secret-123"
}

### Register asking for the admin role → 201, role "user" with adminRequest "pending"
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Grace Planter",
  "email": "grace@example.com",
  "password": "plain-secret-123",
  "requestAdmin": true
}

### Register with invalid data → 400 ValidationError listing every field
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### Log in → 200 with a JWT (run "Register a user" first)
# The token is saved as {{token}} for the protected requests below.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "plain-secret-123"
}

@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

### Log in with a wrong password → 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### Current user → 200 (run "Log in" first)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Current user without a token → 401 Unauthorized
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

### --- Admin requests (log in as an admin first: npm run seed:admin, then "Log in" with ADMIN_*) ---

### Pending admin requests → 200 for an admin, 403 for a regular user
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/admin-requests
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Approve a request → 200, the user becomes admin (replace the id with one from the list)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/000000000000000000000000/admin-request
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "approve" }

### Reject a request → 200 (a second decision on the same user → 409 Conflict)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/000000000000000000000000/admin-request
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "decision": "reject" }

### --- Sensors (any logged-in user can read the catalog) ---

### List sensors → 200 with pagination metadata
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Filter sensors by type and status
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors?type=soil_moisture&active=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Invalid query → 400 listing every wrong parameter
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors?page=0&type=wind
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Sensor detail → 200 (replace the id), 404 if it does not exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/sensors/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Sensor management (admin token required; a regular user gets 403) ---

### Create a sensor → 201 with a Location header
# @name createSensor
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Tomato bed moisture",
  "type": "soil_moisture",
  "location": "Bed 3",
  "threshold": 25,
  "thresholdDirection": "below"
}

@sensorId = {{createSensor.response.body.data.sensor.id}}

### Create a sensor with invalid data → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "type": "wind", "threshold": "high" }

### Update a sensor → 200 (only the fields sent change; readings are re-evaluated
### if threshold or thresholdDirection change)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "threshold": 20, "active": false }

### Delete a sensor → 204 if it has no readings; 409 if it has readings
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Delete a sensor and all its readings → 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}?cascade=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### --- Readings (any logged-in user can record and read them) ---
### Run "Create a sensor" first (threshold 25, direction below) to fill {{sensorId}}.

### Record a normal reading → 201, anomalous: false
# @name createReading
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 31.5, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T10:00:00Z" }

@readingId = {{createReading.response.body.data.reading.id}}

### Record an anomalous reading (below the threshold) → 201, anomalous: true
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/{{sensorId}}/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 12, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T11:00:00Z" }

### Record a reading for a sensor that does not exist → 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/sensors/000000000000000000000000/readings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "value": 12, "timestamp": "2026-10-18T11:00:00Z" }

### Reading detail → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/readings/{{readingId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
